/-!
# The source of the conormal map of Tag 0B3V clause 3 on a chart, read on a generator

`Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictConormalSourceIsoTilde` identifies the source
`ker(q) ⊗ 𝓛^{⊗ -1}` of the conormal map of [Stacks, Tag 0B3V] clause 3, restricted to a chart `W`,
with `(ker p)^~` pulled back along `W ≅ Spec Γ(X, W)`. The sections of that sheaf are generated by
`AlgebraicGeometry.tilde.toOpen` through the unit of `hW.isoSpec.hom^* ⊣ (hW.isoSpec.hom)_*`, which
is what `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.hom_ext_of_unit_toOpen` reduces an equation of
morphisms out of it to. **This file says where the inverse of that identification carries such a
generator**: to the section `k ⊗ s̄^{⊗ -1}` of `ker(q) ⊗ 𝓛^{⊗ -1}` over `W`.

`Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictKernelIsoTilde_inv_unit_toOpen` already carries the
generator back to the section of `ker(q)|_W` that `k` *is*; what was missing is the other factor,
`Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictSourceIso`, on a section — and in the *inverse*
direction, since the generator lies on the `(ker p)^~` side. So most of this file is the
restricted tensor product read on sections: Tag 01CD along `W.ι` carries a product section to a
product section, and the trivialisation of the inverse twist and the right unitor insert the
second factor.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictTensorIso_hom_tensorSectionsAt` and
  `restrictTensorIso_inv_tensorSectionsAt`: **the restricted tensor product on a product
  section**, in both directions. Both sides of
  `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictTensorIso` are generated by the sections determined by
  a pair, and the isomorphism matches them up.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.pullbackTensorComparison_pullbackSection_tensorSectionsAt` and
  `pullbackTensorComparison_inv_tensorSectionsAt`: **Tag 01CD on the pullback of a product
  section**, in both directions.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictSourceIso_inv_tensorSectionsAt`: **the reduction
  `(K ⊗ 𝓛^{⊗ -1})|_W ≅ K|_W` on a section, inverted.** A section `κ` of `K|_W` comes from
  `κ ⊗ s̄^{⊗ -1}`, where `s̄^{⊗ -1}` is the section of the inverse twist that the trivialisation
  names — the value of `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictInverseTwistIso` inverse at `1`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictConormalSourceIsoTilde_inv_unit_toOpen`: **the source
  identification of clause 3 on a chart, read on a generator.** This is the source half of the
  equation the clause reduces to; the target half is
  `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.conormalZeroSectionTildeIso_hom_unit_toOpen`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.surjective_smul_restrictIsoUnit` and
  `notMem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_restrictIsoUnit_inv_one`: **a trivialisation of a restriction
  names a generator.** The section `θ⁻¹(1)` of `M` over `W` that a trivialisation
  `θ : M|_W ≅ 𝒪_W` names generates the sections of `M` over every open inside `W`, and hence —
  for `M` invertible — its germ at every point of `W` escapes `𝔪_y M_y`. At
  `θ = restrictInverseTwistIso Q.L W τ` this is the germ condition the pairing existence of
  [Stacks, Tag 01CY] asks of the generator of `𝓛^{⊗ -1}` that
  `restrictConormalSourceIsoTilde_inv_unit_toOpen` produces.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.notMem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_restrictIsoUnit_res`: **the same
  germ condition for the generator restricted to a smaller open.** The generator lives over
  `W.ι ''ᵁ ⊤`, which is `W` only up to `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.ι_image_top`, so a consumer
  whose remaining data is indexed by `W` meets a restriction of it; germs do not see a
  restriction, so the condition is the same one.

## Implementation notes

The right unitor of the monoidal structure used here is *not*
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.tensorProductRightUnitor`: `monoidalSheafTensor` is
`SheafOfModules.monoidalCategorySheafTensor`, whose constraints are re-seated along
`SheafOfModules.sheafTensorNatIso`, so the section formula
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorSections_rightUnitorAt` does not apply to `ρ_` on the nose and the
crossing is not a `rfl`. `SheafOfModules.rightUnitor_sheafTensor_eq_iso` is the bridge, and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorSheafUnitRightIso_inv_app` is the formula on the far side of it.

Nothing is rewritten, and no composite is split inside a larger term:
`restrictConormalSourceIsoTilde_inv` names the split of the chart identification as an equation of
*morphisms*, which is a `rfl`, whereas the same split stated on a section is a
`maximum recursion depth` error. See the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleConormal.ChartRatio` for why no `rw` occurs on
this layer and those of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleConormal.ChartSourceGenerator` for the discipline
of naming splits.

The opens are not transported. Each formula carries the inequality it needs as a hypothesis
(`h : V ≤ W.ι ⁻¹ᵁ (W.ι ''ᵁ V)`), in the style of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.restrictFunctorIsoPullback_hom_val_app`; the hom-sets of
`TopologicalSpace.Opens` are subsingletons, so which proof is supplied cannot matter, and
`Subsingleton.elim` is what collapses the restriction maps that appear. In particular
`Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.val_map_le_refl` is how the two restrictions
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.restrictFunctorIsoPullback_inv_pullbackSection` leaves
behind are removed.

